# HTTP API

Golden reference: `src/modules/examples/`.

## Purpose

Predictable resource-oriented APIs: plural paths, validated input at the boundary, backend-owned OpenAPI contract.

Path naming, audience prefixes (`/me`, `/employee`, `/admin`), and list query params: **`rest-api-convention.mdc`**. Who may call which surface: **`role-based-access.mdc`**.

## Routes

- Mount modules in `src/app/router.ts`. **No URL version prefix by default** — see `platform-patterns.mdc` before adding `/api/v1`.
- One module = one resource collection (`/examples`, `/uploads`). Role-separated surfaces use audience mounts — do not clone the same CRUD under every prefix.
- List endpoints return `{ items, meta }` with shared pagination helpers.

| Concern | Pattern |
| ------- | ------- |
| Collection | `GET /examples`, `POST /examples` |
| Member | `GET /examples/:id` |
| Pagination | `paginatedQuerySchema` + `pageToOffset` + `buildPaginationMeta` (`page`, `limit`, `sort`, `order`, `search`) |
| Filtering | `search` or explicit filter fields — see `search-query-guidelines.mdc` |
| Sorting | Allowlisted `sort` enum + `order` asc/desc; `parseSortField` in service |
| Count | `Promise.all([findMany, count])` with the **same** `where` |

```ts
// router.ts
apiRouter.use("/examples", examplesRouter);

// routes.ts
examplesRouter.get("/", validateQuery(listExamplesQuerySchema), asyncHandler(listExamplesController));
examplesRouter.get("/:id", validateParams(exampleParamsSchema), asyncHandler(getExampleController));
examplesRouter.post("/", validateBody(createExampleBodySchema), asyncHandler(createExampleController));
```

## Zod validation

Golden reference: `src/middleware/validate.ts`, `src/lib/zod-validation.ts`.

- `validateBody` / `validateQuery` / `validateParams` middleware attaches parsed data to `req`.
- `src/app/env.ts` is the **only** place that parses environment variables.
- On parse failure at the HTTP boundary: middleware calls `validationErrorFromZod(parsed.error)` — never `parsed.error.flatten()` or raw `ZodError.message`.
- `message` is always `"Validation failed"`; per-field copy lives in `errors.fieldErrors` only (humanized via `configureZodErrorMap()` at startup).
- Nested Zod paths flatten to dot keys for the frontend (`identitySummary.builds`) — see `flattenZodError()` in `src/lib/format-zod-error.ts`.
- Service-level or LLM output parses outside middleware: use `validationErrorFromZod(error)` or throw `ValidationError`; `errorHandler` catches stray `ZodError` as a safety net.
- Business rule failures use domain `code` + human `message` (e.g. `CONFLICT` / "Resource conflict") — no `fieldErrors` unless optionally mapping one field.

Example JSON samples: [`docs/api-response-samples.md`](../../../docs/api-response-samples.md).

| Input | Rule |
| ----- | ---- |
| Body | `.strict()` objects |
| Query numbers | `z.coerce.number()` |
| Pagination | Reuse `paginatedQuerySchema` |
| Env | `envSchema.parse(process.env)` in `env.ts` only |

```ts
// routes — validate middleware handles failures; do not hand-roll ValidationError here
examplesRouter.post("/", validateBody(createExampleBodySchema), asyncHandler(createExampleController));

// service — Zod parse outside middleware
const parsed = llmOutputSchema.safeParse(raw);
if (!parsed.success) {
  throw validationErrorFromZod(parsed.error);
}

export const createExampleBodySchema = z.object({ label: z.string().trim().min(1).optional() }).strict();
export const listExamplesQuerySchema = paginatedQuerySchema.extend({
  sort: z.enum(["createdAt", "label"]).optional(),
});
```

## OpenAPI contract

Golden reference: `src/modules/examples/examples.openapi.ts`.

- Register paths per module in `*.openapi.ts`; aggregate in `src/app/openapi.ts`.
- Run `pnpm openapi:generate` after route or schema changes; commit `contracts/openapi.json`.
- The backend owns the API contract; frontends integrate per project without a shared type package.

| Step | Action |
| ---- | ------ |
| 1 | Define shapes in `*.schema.ts` |
| 2 | Register paths in `*.openapi.ts` with query params documented for list routes |
| 3 | `pnpm openapi:generate` → commit `contracts/openapi.json` |

```ts
registry.registerPath({
  method: "get",
  path: "/examples",
  request: { query: listExamplesQuerySchema },
  responses: { 200: { description: "Paginated examples", ... } },
});
```

Frontend types: generate from `contracts/openapi.json` in the frontend repo — do not add shared packages here.

## Good examples

```ts
// service — same where for items and count
const [items, total] = await Promise.all([
  prisma.example.findMany({ where, orderBy, skip, take }),
  prisma.example.count({ where }),
]);
return { items, meta: buildPaginationMeta(query.page, query.limit, total) };
```

## Bad examples

```ts
GET /getExamples
GET /examples?page=1&pageSize=50        // use limit, not pageSize
GET /examples?sort=password              // never allow unvalidated sort fields
const page = Number(req.query.page);      // unvalidated in controller
const body = req.body as CreateExampleBody; // type assertion without parse
ValidationError("…", parsed.error.flatten()) // use validationErrorFromZod instead
throw parsed.error // raw ZodError leaks into message — use validationErrorFromZod
// Hand-editing contracts/openapi.json without regenerating
shared/types.ts or packages/api-types     // cross-repo DTO packages
```

## Explicit prohibitions

- No verb routes (`/createExample`) for CRUD resources.
- No RPC-style paths unless genuinely not resource-shaped (webhooks, actions).
- No unbounded lists — always paginate collection endpoints.
- No `pageSize` / `perPage` / `q` aliases — use `limit` / `search` (`rest-api-convention.mdc`).
- No raw `req.query` / `req.body` in controllers — validate with Zod first.
- No trusting env vars outside `env.ts`.
- Never edit `contracts/openapi.json` by hand except via generator output.
- No raw `ZodError.message` or `parsed.error.flatten()` in API responses — use `validationErrorFromZod`.
- No `shared/`, `dto/`, or cross-repo type packages for API shapes.

## AI guidance

When adding a list endpoint: extend `paginatedQuerySchema`, allowlist sort fields, mirror `examples.service.ts`, document query params in `*.openapi.ts`. New path or role surface: `rest-api-convention.mdc` + `role-based-access.mdc`. Search/filters: `search-query-guidelines.mdc`. Response shapes: `response-contracts.mdc`. Error envelopes and validation samples: `docs/api-response-samples.md`. After any public route or schema change, run `pnpm openapi:generate`. Changing response shapes or removing fields: `api-evolution.mdc`.
